    "done_when": "Establish what the nova forward map, topology read and forward solve cost on the H200 as plasma cell count grows, to judge whether solving accuracy by cell count (about 2,000 cells and upward) is affordable. Done when the report holds: (1) a table of every measured cost against cell count, from existing receipts and run logs: cold compile wall and expanded equation count of the topology read and of the forward solve, warm execute wall per slice (for example the 42.8 ms per slice figure and its cell count), device memory, host RSS, Biot coupling assembly time, and executable size, each with cell count, device and source; (2) the scaling law of each cost in cell count, separating costs that depend on cell count (coupling matrices of size cells squared, linear solves, per-cell membership) from costs that do not (the topology read compile measured flat at about 640 to 772 s across 132 to 550 cells, dominated by the point jet fourth derivative), with the evidence for each; (3) a projection of each cost to 2,000, 5,000, 10,000 and 20,000 cells on one H200 card (141 GB), naming where memory or wall would bind, and which data structures are dense; (4) the one or two H200 measurements that would most cheaply confirm the projection, written as runnable command lines against existing scripts, as follow-ons rather than run here. Work read-only: read plans under docs/plans, research under docs/research, evidence fragments under docs/evidence, receipts and figures under docs/figures and the GPFS evidence root, run directories under /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/runs that belong to project nova, the committed ledger docs/state/nova, and the source under nova/ and tests/. Every number you report carries its source (file path and anchor, or run id and log), and every claim that is an inference rather than a measurement says so. Deliver the report as one markdown file at the assigned write path, with the required tables, and write the manifest with status complete, blocked or failed, which you set yourself.",
